{templateType Trilobit\Core\Presentation\Styleguide\OverviewDefaultTemplate}

{*
 * How wide the content runs, and the one exception a page is allowed to make.
 *
 * The width is the reader's setting, chosen with the switch above this page
 * like the theme and the mode, and every other page of the guide is drawn at
 * it. The exception cannot be shown on a page that follows the setting, so it
 * is a page of its own - the next one in the menu - and this is where it is
 * explained and pointed at. See .ai/plans/09-chrome-a-sirka-obsahu.md, L4.
 *
 * The link is written with n:href rather than handed over resolved: it points
 * at one named page of this same guide, and the router refuses it while the
 * page is being drawn if that page ever stops being listed.
 *}

{block sgPage}
    <p class="l-measure">
        How wide the content of a page runs is chosen with the switch above, the same way the theme
        and the mode are, and it is remembered for the next page. Every page of this guide is drawn at
        whatever was chosen, and so is every page of the application.
    </p>

    <p class="l-measure">
        A page may insist on a width of its own where it has to - a report with a column for every day
        of a month overflows at any width, and cannot wait for somebody to remember to switch:
        <a n:href="page group: 'foundations', page: 'full-width'" data-testid="styleguide-full-width-link">see one that does</a>.
    </p>
{/block}
